quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  19,52,And We called to him from the right side of the Mount and brought him close for intimate communication.
  19,53,"And We granted him, out of Our mercy, his brother Harun (Aaron), as a prophet (to assist him in his mission)."
  19,54,"And mention Isma‘il (Ishmael) in the Book. Indeed, he was truthful to (his) promise and was a messenger (and) a prophet."
  19,55,"He used to enjoin the prayer and almsgiving upon his household, and he was pleasing to his Lord."
  19,56,"And mention Idris in the Book. Indeed, he was a most truthful person (and) a prophet."
  19,57,And We raised him to an exalted station.
  19,58,"They are the ones whom Allah has blessed among the prophets from the progeny of Adam, and from (the progeny of) those (believers) whom We carried with Nuh ([Noah] on the Ark), and from the progeny of Ibrahim (Abraham) and Isra’il (Jacob), and from (the progeny of) those whom We had guided and chosen. When the revelations of the Most-Compassionate (Lord) were recited to them, they would fall down, prostrating and weeping."
  19,59,"Then came after them an evil generation that neglected the prayer and followed (their) base desires. So they will soon encounter the perdition (in the Ghayy Valley of Hell),"
  19,60,"except for those who repent, believe and act righteously. It is they who shall enter Paradise and shall not be wronged in the least."
  19,61,"(They will dwell in) the Gardens of Eternity, which the Most-Compassionate (Lord) has promised to His servants in the (realm of the) Unseen. Indeed, His promise shall come to pass."
  19,62,"They shall not hear in it any vain discourse, but only: ‘Peace!’ And they shall have in it their provision, morning and evening."
  19,63,"That is Paradise, which We will give as an inheritance to those of Our servants who are God-conscious."
  19,64,"And (Jibra’il [Gabriel] said): ‘We do not descend except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs whatever is before us, whatever is behind us and everything in between. And your Lord is not forgetful."
